# Codex review of 332, item 4: the var of the Structure fn creates is copied from the written var through one map in
# which the written var is the new var, keeping the nesting of the copied Structures: Code is under the copy of Box, so
# its kk is Box's own (9) -- the caller's frames hold no kk, and a Code flattened under var would find none. The written
# var of the declaration stays as written.
fn: probe () int (Box: (int: kk 9; Code: (int: r 0; r: kk)))
    call: var\Box\Code var\Box\Code
    return: var\Box\Code\r
end: probe
int: seen probe()
